+
+
+## Ascendant Prismatic Dawn - milestone C
+
+C supersedes A/B's temporary ending. Editable descriptor sections now cover aurora 2600, explosion 400 and card 1500 ms, completing 32,500 ms at Normal (22,750 ms at Fast). The shared engine extends the existing sigil/post passes with 3/4/5 pleated curtain layers, inward history streaks, a pullback/push-in, progressive whitening and a 700 ms chromatic-burst envelope. Shared clock hands acquire shutter trails. A prismatic shockwave, halo and horizontal flare accompany one white flash (110 ms rise, 590 ms decay, peak overlay 0.76). The remaining foreground fades through the first 160 ms of the card flip. GPU resources are disposed at handoff; the final decay and quiet field use Canvas. The title's final inversion mask dissolves through the curtains without a hard reset.
+
+S8 mounts the card at 31,000 ms, flips it directly over 400 ms and materializes from 0.96 to 1 over 1500 ms, with soft bloom and a 1200 ms stroke-dash squircle border reveal. Normal metadata/variant/Keep/Delete sequencing waits until the S8 materialization completes. The finish and retained viewport both sample the same serial-seeded field and continuous, 10 Hz presentation age; no field restart occurs at mount. Pastel side colors interpolate rather than jump, and faded edge splashes retain their seeded 2-3 second cadence. Recovery immediately restores the saved card and quiet field without initializing 3D or replaying the film.
+
+The schema extension adds Cards > Cutscenes > Full / Short / Off before save normalization, giving older saves Full without a schema migration. It applies to every rarity intro through the shared controller. Ascendant Short maps the listed shot lengths (15 seconds plus 1.5 seconds S8 = 16.5 seconds), preserving the clock/title and handoff; Fast applies the existing 70% scale. Other intros use a bounded shortened timeline. Very Low, reduced motion and Off use the three-second light sequence: indigo, a restrained point/sigil with thin rings, the local serif title, then a calm fade to the shared field/card. No GL scene, shake, flash or moving background is used for this alternative.
+
+Compressed modes/timescale overrides reduce pulse/spin phase speeds to keep local pulses at most 2.4 Hz and star rotation at most 2 revolutions/second. Dev Full/Short and the optional safe-flash graph join the existing tools; the graph samples a small copy of the current canvas at 10 Hz only when explicitly enabled. It shows linear-luminance change per second and declared flash count, without another frame loop, runtime network or audio. It is not a photosensitivity certification. auroraRise, flash and cardIn join the existing beat hooks.
+
+Verification remains restricted to a single launch and one Full/Medium/Normal dev-triggered playthrough; no automated tests, screenshots, recording or profiling. Short, Fast, Light, Mono, skip, reload, resize, context loss and other graphics configurations are implemented but do not receive runtime acceptance from that one run.
